  <!-- SHOWER TYPES -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Types of Shower We Install Across Liverpool</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We fit every type of shower in Liverpool homes. Here is how each one works and what suits your home best.</p>

      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Electric showers. Works on any water supply.</strong><p>An electric shower heats cold water as it runs. It uses its own heating part inside. No need for hot water from your boiler. It works even when the boiler is broken. The top pick for Liverpool homes with low water pressure or a gravity-fed system. We fit 7.5kW, 9.5kW and 10.8kW units. We suggest 9.5kW or higher for a strong flow.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Hot and cold mixer showers. The basic mixer option.</strong><p>A basic hot and cold mixer takes hot and cold water and mixes them at the valve. No thermostat inside. It needs both hot and cold supplies. The temperature can dip when someone runs another tap. Cheaper than a thermostatic mixer. Supply and fit from £200.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Thermostatic mixer showers. The safest pick for families.</strong><p>A thermostatic bar valve mixes hot and cold water to your set temperature. It holds that temperature even when someone runs a tap in the kitchen. The anti-scald feature makes these showers the safest pick for kids and older people. We supply and fit from £300. Valve, head and riser rail all in.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Power showers. Boost low pressure systems.</strong><p>A power shower has its own pump inside to boost water pressure. Best for homes with a gravity-fed system where the pressure is too low. You need a hot water cylinder for this. It will not work with a combi boiler. Very common in older Liverpool homes with gravity-fed systems. Supply and fit from £350.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Dual head systems. Overhead and handheld in one.</strong><p>A dual outlet system gives you both an overhead shower head and a handheld shower from one valve. Switch between the two with a diverter. Or use both at once. Great for rinsing hair, washing kids or cleaning the shower tray. Supply and fit from £400 including the valve and both heads.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Rainfall heads. The full-body flow.</strong><p>A rainfall head is a large overhead shower head. The water falls straight down like rain. Most rainfall heads are 200mm to 400mm across. They give a soft, full-body flow at the right pressure. Best with mains-pressure water or a power shower system. Supply and fit from £450 including the valve.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Digital showers. The precise tech option.</strong><p>A digital shower lets you set the temperature to the exact degree. You control it from a pad on the wall or from a phone app. Wired or wireless. Common in bigger Liverpool homes and en suites. Supply and fit from £500 for the valve and controller.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Walk-in showers. No tray, level access.</strong><p>A walk-in shower uses a linear drain and a level tiled floor. No shower tray. The walls and floor have to be fully tanked before tiling. We do the full job, start to finish. Tanking. Tiling. The shower valve. Walk-in areas without a tray from £800 supply and fit. Tiling is included.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Shower over bath. Best for small homes.</strong><p>A shower over the bath with a folding screen is the best fix for small Liverpool homes or rentals. Space stays tight. We fit an electric shower over the bath from £200. Or a thermostatic bar valve over the bath from £250. Bath screens from £150 supply and fit.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- NEW: SHOWER BRAND TIERS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">SHOWER BRAND GUIDE</span>
      <h2>Shower Brands We Fit. Budget, Mid and Premium.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">We fit showers across every price tier. Pick the right brand for your budget and your home. Here is what we fit most often in Liverpool homes.</p>

      <!-- BUDGET TIER -->
      <div style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3 style="color:var(--navy);font-size:1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Budget Tier: Triton and Bristan</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.6;">Budget shower brands give you a solid, reliable shower at the lowest price. Best for rental homes, holiday lets and second bathrooms. Triton and Bristan lead the budget tier in the UK. Both have strong parts back-up. Both have been on the market for many years. Spare parts stay easy to get.</p>
        <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:1rem;">
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Triton</strong><p>UK heritage brand. Electric showers from £80 unit cost. Easy to fit. Top picks are the Exe, T80 and T90SR. Spare parts are sold in every UK plumbing shop.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Bristan</strong><p>UK brand, founded in 1977. Top picks are the Frenzy, Smile and Glee ranges. Bar mixers, electric showers and bath fillers all in one range.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- MID TIER -->
      <div style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <h3 style="color:var(--navy);font-size:1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Mid Tier: Mira and Aqualisa</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.6;">Mid-tier brands give you better build, longer life and stronger flow than budget kit. Most family homes in Liverpool sit in this tier. Mira and Aqualisa are the two UK leaders here. Both run their own parts networks. Both have been making showers for decades.</p>
        <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:1rem;">
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Mira</strong><p>UK brand from Gloucestershire. The most-fitted shower in the UK. Sport Max, Elite and Vie are the top picks. Electric, mixer and digital all in the range. Strong limescale defence.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Aqualisa</strong><p>UK brand. They made the first digital shower for UK homes. Quartz and Visage Q are the top picks. Many models have wireless control.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Bristan concealed mixer range</strong><p>Neat looks. Lower price than the German brands. A good fit for mid-tier bathroom suites.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- PREMIUM TIER -->
      <div style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <h3 style="color:var(--navy);font-size:1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Premium Tier: Hansgrohe, Grohe, Crosswater and Vado</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.6;">Premium brands give you the best looks, the best flow and the longest life. Best for new bathroom fits and main bathrooms in higher-end homes. Hansgrohe and Grohe are the German leaders. Crosswater and Vado lead from the UK side. All have brass bodies, ceramic cartridges and warranties of five years or more.</p>
        <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:1rem;">
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Hansgrohe</strong><p>German brand. A world leader in shower design. Ecostat and Raindance Select are the top picks. Both have rainfall heads and dual-head options.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Grohe</strong><p>German brand from 1936. The most-fitted premium shower in UK hotels. The Grohtherm 1000 and the Rainshower are the top picks. SmartControl push-button is a Grohe-only feature.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Crosswater</strong><p>UK premium brand. The Mike Pro and Union ranges lead. Strong on dual-outlet systems.</p></div></div>
          <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Vado</strong><p>UK premium brand. Origins and Velo are the top picks. Modern looks. Good value at the premium end.</p></div></div>
