  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Signs Your Liverpool Shower Needs Replacing or Repairing</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Most shower problems can be fixed without a full swap. We check before we suggest any work.</p>

      <div class="pf-signs" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>Temperature jumps when taps run elsewhere</strong><p>Shower goes scalding hot or freezing cold when someone runs a tap in the kitchen? The thermostatic valve cartridge is worn. A new cartridge from £100 sorts this. No need to swap the whole shower.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>Poor water pressure from the shower head</strong><p>Limescale build-up in the head is the most common cause. A new shower head from £30 often fixes it. If the pressure is poor at every tap, the issue is the water supply or pump, not the shower.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>Electric shower trips the circuit breaker</strong><p>An electric shower that trips the RCD has a failed heating part or water inside the unit. The shower has to be swapped. The heating parts cannot be fixed. We carry common units in the van and can often fit a new one on the same visit.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>Shower valve leaking from body or cartridge</strong><p>A leak from the body or cartridge of the valve can often be fixed with a new cartridge or O-ring seal. We find the source of the leak first. Then we tell you if a fix or a swap is the right call.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>Shower tray cracked or leaking</strong><p>A cracked shower tray has to go. It cannot be fixed for the long term. A leaking tray can damage the floor below. This is a real risk in Liverpool's old terraced homes with timber joists. We swap shower trays from £200 labour.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>Shower over 10 years old with faults</strong><p>Electric showers tend to last 5 to 10 years. A unit over 10 years old with faults is often cheaper to swap than fix. Spare parts get harder to find after 8 to 10 years.</p></div></div>
      </div>

      <div style="background:#f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1.5rem;text-align:center;margin-top:2rem;">
