      <h2>Shower Installation Liverpool. Your Questions Answered.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Straight answers to what Liverpool homeowners ask most before they book.</p>
      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does shower installation cost in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Electric showers from £200 supply and fit. Hot-cold mixer from £200. Thermostatic mixer from £300. Power shower from £350. Digital shower from £500. Walk-in shower areas from £800. Rainfall head systems from £450. Dual-head systems from £400. We give a free written quote before any work starts.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">TYPES</span>&nbsp; What is the best type of shower for a Liverpool home?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>It comes down to your water supply. Electric showers work on any system. They are the most common pick in Liverpool. Thermo mixers are best for homes with good pressure. Power showers boost low pressure. Digital showers give the best control. We advise at the free quote visit.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">BRANDS</span>&nbsp; What shower brands do you fit?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We fit Triton, Bristan, Mira, Aqualisa, Hansgrohe, Grohe, Crosswater and Vado. Budget, mid-tier and premium ranges. We can supply the shower or fit one you have bought. Tell us your budget and what matters to you. We help you pick the right brand for your home.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">DUAL HEAD</span>&nbsp; Can you fit a dual head shower system?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. A dual outlet system gives you both an overhead shower head and a handheld one. Switch between them or use both at the same time. We fit dual outlet systems from £400 supply and fit. Hansgrohe, Grohe and Crosswater all have strong dual outlet ranges.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">RAINFALL</span>&nbsp; Can you fit a rainfall shower head?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. A rainfall head is a large overhead shower head, often 200mm to 400mm across. The flow falls down like rain. It works best with mains-pressure water or a power shower system. We supply and fit from £450. Hansgrohe Raindance and Grohe Rainshower are the top picks here.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">BATH</span>&nbsp; Can you fit a shower over a bath?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Electric shower over bath from £200 supply and fit. Thermostatic bar valve over bath from £250. Bath screens from £150 supply and fit. A shower over bath is a good fix for smaller Liverpool homes or rentals where space is tight.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">TIME</span>&nbsp; How long does shower installation take?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A like-for-like electric shower swap takes 2 to 3 hours. A new thermostatic mixer fit takes 2 to 4 hours. A shower tray and enclosure takes 1 day. A full walk-in tiled shower area takes 2 to 3 days. We tell you the time at the quote stage.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">ELECTRICIAN</span>&nbsp; Do you have an in-house electrician for electric showers?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We have a Part P NICEIC qualified electrician on the team via our sister firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a>. All electrical work is done in-house. No subs. The plumbing and the wiring get done on the same visit. This means we can fit electric showers, change shower circuits and upgrade the cable for high-kW units all in one visit.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are you Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We are Gas Safe registered. All plumbing work is done by our own engineers. You can verify us at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. We never use subs.</p></div></details>
